From 61d86d08b393b7ec8544bff77aef07fdfb4e33c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kunstbanause <3209654+Kunstbanause@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:36:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] d/rift_s: Camera images for passthrough, Oculus button
 long press

Add xrt_device::get_passthrough_frames: the latest camera images, their
capture time, camera poses relative to the head and Fisheye62
intrinsics, plus a "forced" flag for passthrough the user switched on.
Devices without it return XRT_ERROR_NOT_IMPLEMENTED (silently, the
compositor polls it every frame).

The Rift S hands out the two front cameras (left eye: front left,
right eye: front right). They are copied out of the camera frame into
frames of their own, so the v4l2 buffers are not held, and only while
someone asked for images in the last 500 ms. Images older than 500 ms
are not handed out (camera stream stopped).

Holding the Oculus button on the right controller for 600 ms toggles
the forced flag (RIFT_S_PASSTHROUGH_HOLD_MS, 0 disables). Short presses
still go to apps. The debug UI has a toggle too, and the status file
gets "passthrough": {forced, streaming, frame_age_ms}.

The HMD now also offers the alpha blend environment mode, after opaque
so apps keep defaulting to opaque.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
